Runtime deps declared in cpanfile diverge from lib/ in both directions.

Loaded but undeclared:
  Moose                              API.pm (the plugin class itself)
  Dist::Zilla::Role::BeforeBuild     API.pm, composed for the engine precheck
  namespace::autoclean               API.pm
  Carp                               Client.pm

Declared but never loaded:
  Archive::Tar::Wrapper              nothing uses it; _create_tar in Client.pm
                                     does a runtime require of Archive::Tar

Moo is correctly declared and used by Client/Result/TagTemplate. Note the mixed
object system is deliberate: Dist::Zilla::Role::Plugin forces Moose on API.pm,
the three helper classes carry no Dist::Zilla dependency and stay Moo.

A naive "^use" scan misses Archive::Tar because it is a lazy require.

Fixed: cpanfile now declares Moose, Dist::Zilla::Role::BeforeBuild, namespace::autoclean, Carp, Archive::Tar and Test::Warnings; Archive::Tar::Wrapper dropped. The lazy require of Archive::Tar in _create_tar was hoisted to a top-level use (house rule: require is not a lazy optimization). List sorted alphabetically.
